  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-PMR26-IRQ180</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Extended social protection coverage and established social protection floor</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ILO supports the extension of social protection coverage in Iraq through two complementary policy tracks under the European Union&#x2013;United Nations Joint Programme on Social Protection. In the Kurdistan Region of Iraq (KRI), the ILO facilitated the development of the Social Security Extension Strategy 2025&#x2013;2030 through a structured Technical Working Group (TWG) process involving the Ministry of Labour and Social Affairs in the Kurdistan Region of Iraq, social partners, and relevant ministries. The Strategy defines pathways for extending coverage to private sector workers, the informal economy, and agriculture, while integrating capacity-building and awareness-raising components.
At the federal level, the ILO provided technical inputs to Iraq&apos;s national Social Protection Strategy 2026&#x2013;2030 led by the Ministry of Planning. The combined interventions aim to establish a social protection floor in line with Convention No. 102 and Recommendation No. 202.</narrative>
  </description>
